{
  "summary": "Allows descriptor imports into private-key-enabled wallets when the descriptor lacks private keys, provided the wallet already holds them. The wallet inspects the descriptor's pubkeys and xpubs with key origins, matches them against known private keys and master xprvs across its descriptor managers, and substitutes them into the descriptor before import.",
  "problem": "Currently, importing descriptors into a private-key-enabled wallet fails unless the descriptor explicitly contains the private keys. This forces users to expose private key material during RPC imports even when the wallet already holds the corresponding xprv or private key from an existing descriptor.",
  "evidence": [
    "Closes issue #27336: 'Should be able to import an xpub descriptor to a privkey-enabled wallet if the wallet has the privkeys'",
    "PR description: 'Currently importing a descriptor to a wallet that has private keys requires the descriptor to include the private keys. This is not ideal as it means exposing private key material.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#34861"
    ],
